-### Algorithm: Lifting Scheme Implementation
-The transform is applied separably along each axis using a lifting scheme [S1]. The forward transform computes the detail (high-pass) and approximation (low-pass) subbands using the following formulas:
-$$O_{new}[i] = O[i] - G \sum_{j} c_{P,j} \cdot E[i - k_j]$$
-$$E_{new}[i] = E[i] + U \sum_{j} c_{U,j} \cdot O_{new}[i - k_j]$$
-where $E$ and $O$ are the even and odd samples of the input signal, and $k_j, c_{P,j}, c_{U,j}$ are the offsets and coefficients for the prediction and update steps [S1]. The following pseudocode implements a single 1D pass for a given kernel configuration:
